{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider's route-deviation claim fails at the first gate. The governing distance is the GPS polyline, gps_trace.trace_distance_km 31.49 km — trip_record.actual_distance_km 31.5 km is the rounded convenience copy of the same measurement and may NOT be cited for the threshold test — measured against the booked optimal of 28.0 km. That is an excess of 3.49 km, or 12.46% of optimal. POL-RD-01 requires the excess to be BOTH greater than 20% of optimal AND greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms; 12.46% fails the percentage limb decisively, so no deviation is established and, on the clause's own words, the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00532", "EV-TRIP-00532"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The excess is not merely below the establishment gate, it is nowhere near material. 3.49 km is far under the 8.0 km absolute materiality figure and 12.46% is far under the 50% figure, so the deviation is neither established nor material and POL-RD-06's repeat-pattern enquiry is never engaged on this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00532", "EV-TRIP-00532"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if that enquiry were engaged, no repeat-deviation pattern is available against this driver: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 and driver_profile.completed_trips_90d is 250, short of both the three-flag test and the 0.05 ratio test, so none of POL-RD-06's three effects can follow. The clause is explicit that a pattern may never be used to establish that this particular trip deviated — that finding must rest on this trip's trace alone, and this trip's trace is under the threshold.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00532"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-RD-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and limb (b) requires an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold measured from an unimpaired trace. This trace is unimpaired for policy purposes: 289 fixes at a 10-second cadence over the 48-minute trip, 100% coverage, no gaps recorded, and a maximum inter-fix gap of 0.0 s, so none of POL-RD-07 limbs (a) to (c) is met. Limb (b) therefore fails, the burden never shifts, and the driver is never required to point to any exculpatory artifact at all.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00532", "EV-TRIP-00532"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This trip is priced UPFRONT_QUOTE: quoted_fare_sgd is 75.00 and fare_model is UPFRONT_QUOTE. Under POL-RD-11 POL-RD-02 does not run and no distance-or-time refund is available to the rider however large the excess, because the distance and time charges were fixed at booking and the rider was already whole on those lines. On this fare model the ordinary consequence of a detour is a cost borne by the driver, not a refund to the rider — the rider cannot recover the upside of a risk the pricing model never placed on him.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00532"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fare_model",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's appeal to other riders who 'got a full refund for less', and the request for the whole 81.00, has no clause behind it. POL-RD-11 limits the remedy on an upfront-quoted trip to the arithmetic difference between charged_total and quoted_fare_sgd plus the pass-through and statutory lines properly chargeable under POL-RD-09. There is no parity entitlement between cases and no discretionary round-number payment anywhere in this policy; the figure is fixed by the clause, not by comparison with strangers.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00532"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's premise that 'the platform refunded half' is not in the record at all: the fare ledger records payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so no refund has been issued on this trip and nothing has been reversed. NO_ACTION under POL-GEN-03 is party-relative — it leaves payment_status and refund_issued_sgd exactly as they stand — and on a rider-filed dispute over a charge that still stands, that means the charge stands.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00532"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's second complaint — that the driver 'picked someone else up when I paid for a solo ride' — is not a ground of refund under this policy. The booking is a RYDE_X trip, and POL-RD-12, the only clause that addresses distance attributable to collecting or setting down a co-rider, applies where trip_record.vehicle_type is RYDE_POOL; it is not RYDE_POOL here. The chat log for this trip holds 0 messages and no artifact in the bundle records a second pickup, so an assertion that cites no evidence ID carries no weight under POL-RD-08. In any event the fare was fixed at booking, so any extra time on the road did not change what the rider paid (POL-RD-11).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00532", "EV-CHAT-00532"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even on the rider's best case the money is small and capped. The rider paid charged_total 81.00 against a quoted_fare_sgd of 75.00, and the entire 6.00 difference is a single ERP line. POL-RD-11(a) refunds only the excess of charged_total over the quoted fare plus pass-through lines 'actually crossed' under POL-RD-09; the platform's own comparison puts the trace's closest approach to that gantry at 1,159 m, well outside the POL-RD-09(4) crossing radius, so that 6.00 can only travel as a pass-through correction. The driver does not resist that 6.00 — it is government-set ERP, never driver revenue — but it is the ceiling: the remaining 75.00 of the rider's claim is the quoted fare he agreed to, and it fails on POL-RD-01, POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-11.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00532", "EV-GPS-00532"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "properly_chargeable.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 6.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity review: the CTE (Ang Mo Kio Ave 1 towards City) ERP line of SGD 6.00 on TRP-00532 was charged although the GPS trace never crossed that gantry (closest fix 1,159.02 m away, outside the 250 m match radius POL-RD-09(4) applies); the line is refunded in full as a standalone correction and is referred for billing-integrity review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. This is a route-deviation dispute over trip TRP-00532, priced as an UPFRONT_QUOTE (fare_breakdown.fare_model) with quoted_fare_sgd 75.00 and charged_total 81.00. The rider contests the whole 81.00.\n\nDistance (driver's point accepted). POL-RD-01 governs, and the GPS trace governs the measurement. The trace figure is gps_trace.trace_distance_km 31.49 km against a booked optimal of 28.00 km, an excess of 3.49 km or 12.46% of optimal. Both establishment limbs must pass — more than 20% and more than 0.8 km — and 12.46% fails decisively, so no route deviation is established and POL-RD-06 is never engaged. Independently, POL-RD-11 provides that on an upfront-quoted trip POL-RD-02 does not run and the distance and time charges were fixed at booking, so no distance-or-time refund is available however the trip is characterised. The rider's own advocate does not press for one.\n\nPass-through lines (rider's point accepted in part). The only difference between the 75.00 quoted fare and the 81.00 charged total is a single 6.00 ERP line for the CTE (Ang Mo Kio Ave 1 towards City) gantry. The trace's nearest fix to that gantry is 1,159.02 m away, far outside the 250 m crossing radius POL-RD-09(4) applies, and the line is carried crossed:false. A charge for a gantry the trace never passes is a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4), refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not a deviation exists; POL-RD-11(a) reaches the same figure, 81.00 less quoted fare 75.00 less 0.00 properly chargeable (no crossed ERP, no airport surcharge on a non-airport trip, waiting_time_fee 0.00). That is one sum of 6.00, not two, and it is the whole of the amount payable. It is not a parity award: no clause permits comparison with other cases, and the figure comes off the fare ledger.\n\nDriver's traffic excuse. 'Local roads were faster that day' asserts an external traffic cause. Under POL-RD-13 it is tested only against the traffic_advisory for this trip, and EV-ADVIS-00532-01 is MISSING — weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, no payload. The comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08; it neither reduces the excess nor supplies an amended optimal. Because the driver cited no advisory identifier, this is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, and it is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. Disclosure under POL-GEN-02(3): the ruling notes the absent advisory, but no finding rests on it as a carrier — a MISSING artifact can carry no fact, and the deciding facts rest on full-weight artifacts.\n\nSecond passenger. The trip_record records vehicle_type RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's pooled-itinerary exclusion does not apply to this booking. The driver's statement that 'the other passenger was a short hop' is on the record; because the fare was fixed at booking, it changed nothing the rider paid and produces no monetary outcome under this policy. It remains an open question for the human reviewer and is noted here rather than raised as a referral, as no clause directs one.\n\nRecord check. The rider's belief that the platform refunded half is not supported: the ledger shows payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so the charge still stands and this ruling is the first money to move.\n\nOther matters. The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes (289 fixes at a 10 s cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, maximum inter-fix gap 0.0 s), so neither POL-RD-07 nor POL-RD-10(3) is engaged. The in-app chat log is empty, so POL-RD-04 cannot be run. Trip identifiers match across the trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown and no timestamp contradiction arises, so no POL-RD-10 trigger fires. Confidence 0.90 is capped by the weight_multiplier of the artifacts carrying the deciding facts — the GPS trace EV-GPS-00532 and the fare ledger EV-FARE-00532, both 1.0 — and sits above the 0.70 floor."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 6.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: the CTE (Ang Mo Kio Ave 1 towards City) ERP line of SGD 6.00 on EV-FARE-00532 was charged for a gantry the GPS trace never crossed (closest approach 1,159.02 m, outside the 250 m crossing radius; the ledger itself records the line as crossed: false). The line is refunded in full as a standalone correction and is logged here as a billing-integrity finding."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.93,
    "explanation": "Both parties: the disputed amount is the difference between what was charged (charged_total SGD 81.00) and the fare quoted at booking (quoted_fare_sgd SGD 75.00), and it turns on a single SGD 6.00 ERP line, not on the route. The rider recovers SGD 6.00; the rest of the SGD 81.00 claim fails.\n\nDistance. The governing measurement is the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00532, trace_distance_km 31.49 km), not the trip record's rounded copy (EV-TRIP-00532, actual_distance_km 31.5 km, which POL-RD-01 forbids citing for the threshold test). Against the booked optimal of 28.00 km that is an excess of 3.49 km, or 12.46%. POL-RD-01 requires an excess of more than 20% AND more than 0.8 km; 12.46% fails the percentage gate, so no deviation is established and none is material. The driver's profile shows no repeat pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 250), so POL-RD-06 does not engage and no conduct referral arises under POL-RD-06(c).\n\nFare model. The trip is UPFRONT_QUOTE (EV-FARE-00532, quoted_fare_sgd 75.00), so POL-RD-11 governs and POL-RD-02 does not run: the distance and time lines were fixed at booking and no distance-or-time refund is available to the rider however large the excess. That is why the 3.49 km of extra driving moves no money here.\n\nWhat survives. The fare ledger charges SGD 6.00 for the CTE (Ang Mo Kio Ave 1 towards City) gantry, but the trace's closest approach to that gantry is 1,159.02 m, far outside the 250 m match radius of POL-RD-09(4), and the ledger's own comparison records the line as crossed: false. Under POL-RD-09(4) a gantry the trace never passes is a phantom line, refunded in full as a standalone correction available whether or not a deviation exists. The refund is therefore charged_total 81.00 less quoted_fare 75.00 less pass-through lines properly chargeable (0.00) = SGD 6.00. The driver does not resist this figure and correctly notes that ERP is government-set, not driver revenue.\n\nRider's second complaint. The driver's statement admits a second passenger on a trip recorded as RYDE_X, a solo product. POL-RD-12's co-rider exclusion applies only where trip_record.vehicle_type is RYDE_POOL, so it gives no refund on this booking, and because the fare was fixed at booking the extra passenger did not change what the rider paid. No clause in this policy refunds a solo booking for a co-passenger, so no money turns on it; the admission is recorded but produces no payment and no clause-mandated referral.\n\nDriver's traffic explanation. 'Local roads were faster that day' asserts an external traffic cause. Under POL-RD-13 that assertion is tested against the traffic advisory for this trip and nothing else; no advisory covers this window (EV-ADVIS-00532-01 is MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-RD-03 is unavailable, the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08, and it supplies neither a reduction of the excess nor an amended optimal route. Because the driver named no advisory evidence ID, POL-RD-13(1) makes this a gap in the bundle, not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation; the trace is unimpaired (289 fixes at 10 s cadence, zero gaps), so POL-RD-10(3) does not apply either.\n\nConfidence. The deciding figures rest on full-weight artifacts: the charged total of 81.00 and quoted fare of 75.00 on EV-FARE-00532 (weight 1.0), and the gantry non-crossing on EV-GPS-00532 (weight 1.0). The cap is 1.0 and the ruling sits above the 0.70 floor, so no escalation is required. The one referral rides with the money and does not displace it."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 6.00,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity — the SGD 6.00 ERP charge for the CTE (Ang Mo Kio Ave 1 towards City) gantry was billed for a gantry this trip's GPS trace never crossed (closest fix 1,159.02 m away, outside the POL-RD-09(4) 250 m crossing radius, ledger line carried crossed:false); refunded in full as a billing-integrity correction and referred for review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. The trip was booked on an upfront quote of SGD 75.00 and charged SGD 81.00; the SGD 6.00 difference is the single ERP line. Because fare_model is UPFRONT_QUOTE, POL-RD-11 governs: the distance and time charges were fixed at booking, POL-RD-02 does not run, and no distance-or-time refund is available however long the route ran. On route deviation both sides are right and agree: the governing distance is the GPS polyline at 31.49 km (trip_record.actual_distance_km 31.5 km is the rounded copy and may not be cited for the threshold test), against the booked optimal of 28.00 km — an excess of 3.49 km, or 12.46%. POL-RD-01 requires both limbs; 12.46% fails the 20% test, so no deviation is established and no materiality or POL-RD-06 repeat-pattern enquiry is engaged. The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes (289 fixes at 10 s cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps), so POL-RD-07 and POL-RD-10(3) are not triggered. The refundable money is the ERP line. The trace's closest approach to the CTE (Ang Mo Kio Ave 1 towards City) gantry is 1,159.02 m, far outside the 250 m crossing radius POL-RD-09(4) applies, and the ledger itself records the line as crossed:false. A charge for a gantry the trace never passes is a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4) and is refunded in full whether or not a deviation exists. As that line is not properly chargeable, the amount by which the SGD 81.00 charged exceeds the SGD 75.00 quoted fare — SGD 6.00 — is refunded under POL-RD-11(a); the ledger's own pol_rd_11_remedy field publishes the same 6.00. This is the ceiling of the claim, as the driver's advocate conceded: the remaining SGD 75.00 is the quoted fare the rider agreed to and fails on POL-RD-01, POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-11. The driver's explanation that 'local roads were faster that day' asserts an external traffic cause; under POL-RD-13 it is tested only against a traffic_advisory for this trip, and EV-ADVIS-00532-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, no payload), so POL-RD-03 is unavailable and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08 — though the absence is not an escalation under POL-RD-10(5), because the driver named no advisory ID to invoke. The rider's second complaint, that a second passenger was carried on a solo booking, is not a ground of refund: POL-RD-12 applies only to a RYDE_POOL matched itinerary and this booking is RYDE_X, and because the fare was fixed at booking any extra time on the road did not change what was paid. There is no parity entitlement to other cases and no discretionary payment anywhere in the policy, and the record shows payment_status CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00 — no refund has yet been issued on this trip. Every deciding fact is carried by artifacts at weight 1.0 (the GPS trace and the fare breakdown), so confidence rests at 0.9."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
